From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erhan Bilgili <erhan.bilgili@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 01:13:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 24/49] winewayland: Use punch-through compositing for child
 content.

Client and dmabuf child content used to be reconciled with GDI by copying
child pixels into driver-owned overlay subsurfaces. That made the Wayland
driver query window-tree state with NtUser from the wrong side of the lock
boundary and left the driver with a second cached view of child geometry
and z-order.

Instead keep the server/win32u window tree as the source of truth. Let
client subsurfaces toggle parent surface clipping, extend the server
surface region walk to subtract visible self-presenting descendants
and stack client/dmabuf subsurfaces below the parent GDI surface so the
punched-through regions reveal the producer content.

This removes the copy-overlay snapshot path, avoids driver-side child
tree pulls, fixes the client-vs-dmabuf stacking race, and keeps pure
producer windows mapped with a transparent carrier until real parent
contents exist.

Fixes EA Launcher crash during start.
